Level 3 operators
-----------------

 [X] shfill (sampled functions at byte depths; FunctionTypes 0, 2 and
     3 -- the type 4 calculator functions rangecheck, and functions of
     more than one input are served by type 0 only)
 [X] composite fonts (FMapTypes 2 through 8 over any descendants,
     and FMapType 9 through composefont with CIDFont descendants of
     CIDFontType 2, incremental GlyphDirectory delivery, and
     CIDFontType 0, charstrings through StartData; escapes select
     within one modal level; cshow rebinds a CMap composite to
     one-byte codes. The CIDInit procedure set is complete: notdef
     mappings and usematrix are taken, though a single-descendant job
     applies neither)
 [X] setsmoothness, currentsmoothness (recorded only)
 [X] findcolorrendering (names the default instance, whose entries
     describe the conversion a graphics state starts out performing)
 [X] Type 4 CIDFonts, and the BitmapFontInit procedure set: addglyph,
     removeall, removeglyphs (charpath over such a font marks nothing,
     as the language requires)
 [/] FontSetInit procedure set: StartData reads its data and defines
     no FontSet, so a font a document sends this way is unavailable;
     findresource reports the set undefined. Compact font format
     containers are not read
 [X] implicit resource categories: a program may ask what this
     interpreter can do -- ShadingType, FunctionType, HalftoneType,
     ImageType, PatternType, FormType, ColorRenderingType, Filter,
     ColorSpaceFamily and IODevice answer for what is implemented.
     FontType and FMapType are NOT declared, so a program asking after
     a font type is answered undefined rather than truthfully

